# Ooda CLI — argv Dispatch

File: cli/docs/argv.oot

The `ooda` binary parses argv in `cli/main.oo` and dispatches to one of 13+ subcommands. The dispatch is a single match expression:

| argv[0]      | Calls into                                  | Result |
|--------------|---------------------------------------------|--------|
| `build`      | `cli/build/host_build.oo::run_oodac_build`  | Ok(0)  |
| `run`        | `cli/build/host_build.oo::run_oodac_run`    | Ok(0)  |
| `gen`        | `cli/build/gen.oo::run_ooda_gen`            | Ok(0)  |
| `test`       | `cli/build/test.oo::run_ooda_test`          | Ok(0)  |
| `install`    | `cli/build/install.oo::run_ooda_install_cmd`| Ok(0)  |
| `bench`      | `cli/build/bench.oo::run_ooda_bench`        | Ok(0)  |
| `init`       | `cli/build/init.oo::cli_init_project`       | Result |
| `context`    | `cli/build/context.oo::run_ooda_context`    | Ok(0)  |
| `health`     | `cli/build/health.oo::run_ooda_health`      | Ok(0)  |
| `fix`        | `cli/fix/fix.oo::run_ooda_fix`              | Ok(0)  |
| `digest`     | `cli/fix/digest.oo::run_ooda_digest`        | Ok(0)  |
| `fmt`        | `cli/fmt/fmt.oo::run_ooda_fmt`              | Ok(Int)|
| `token`      | `cli/token/cmd_token.oo::run_ooda_token`    | Ok(0)  |
| `opm`        | spawn `opm` (subprocess)                    | Result |
| `lsp`        | spawn `lsp` (subprocess)                    | Result |
| `mcp`        | spawn `mcp` (subprocess)                    | Result |
| (other)      | print help                                  | Err    |

## Why spawn (not link)?

Spawning keeps the 3 packages (opm, lsp, mcp) version-independent. The `ooda` binary does NOT need to be re-released when one of them updates. Each package has its own VERSION and its own release cadence.
